  comparisonBefore: "TypeScript can express possible absence with string | undefined. The === undefined check keeps an empty string separate from an unset value.",
  comparisonAfter: "This small task is already concise in TypeScript. Seseragi Maybe supplies a shared type and operations for present or missing results returned by different lookups and input-handling functions.",
  details: [
    "A in Maybe<A> is the contained type, String here. A Maybe value represents an already-obtained result; it is not an instruction that runs a lookup or calculation.",
    "Handling only Just and omitting Nothing makes match fail with SES-T0301. Choose Either when the caller also needs a reason why there is no successful value."
